    "final_answer": "I have found all the necessary information. Here is the answer to the task:\n\n## The Most Recent UEFA Champions League Final\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article for the 2026 UEFA Champions League final, here are the details:\n\n- **When:** **30 May 2026**\n- **Where:** **Puskás Aréna, Budapest, Hungary**\n- **Winner:** **Paris Saint-Germain (PSG)** defeated Arsenal 4–3 on penalties after a 1–1 draw in extra time\n\n### Additional Details:\n- This was the final match of the **2025–26 UEFA Champions League** (the 71st season of Europe's premier club tournament, and the 34th since it was renamed from the European Cup)\n- PSG were the defending champions going into the match, making this the first final to include a titleholder team since 2018\n- It was PSG's **second UEFA Champions League title**, making them the second club to win back-to-back titles in the Champions League era (matching Real Madrid's 2016–17 feat)\n- **Man of the Match:** Vitinha (Paris Saint-Germain)\n- **Attendance:** 61,035\n- **Referee:** Daniel Siebert (Germany)\n\nAs winners, Paris Saint-Germain earned the right to play in the **2026 UEFA Super Cup** against Aston Villa (winners of the 2025–26 UEFA Europa League) and qualified for the **2029 FIFA Club World Cup**.",
